prompt:
You are a compliance referee. Explain this cross-department gap to a launch manager in 2-3 plain sentences and give 2-3 concrete fix options. Use ONLY these facts; do not invent any.
Seam type: data_residency_breach
Title: 3 supplier(s) process customer data outside UK/EEA, against the customer terms
Departments: Finance, Legal, Product
Facts: {"allowed_regions": ["UK", "EEA"], "breaches": ["V002 StreamLedger Inc: customer payment data processed in US-East (United States); C-2026-031 DPA signed=True", "V007 VerifyPoint Inc: customer identity data processed in US-East (United States); C-2026-045 DPA signed=True", "V003 Harbor Analytics Inc: customer payment data processed in US-East (United States); C-2025-020 DPA signed=False"], "promise": "Customer payment data is processed and stored only within the UK or EEA, including by sub-processors."}
Return JSON: {"explanation": str, "fix_options": [str]}

response:
```json
{
  "explanation": "Our customer terms promise that customer payment data is processed and stored only within the UK or EEA, including by sub-processors, but three suppliers process customer data in US-East (United States). StreamLedger Inc (V002) and Harbor Analytics Inc (V003) handle customer payment data there, and VerifyPoint Inc (V007) handles customer identity data there. StreamLedger and VerifyPoint have signed DPAs (C-2026-031 and C-2026-045), while Harbor Analytics' DPA (C-2025-020) is not signed, so this gap sits across Finance, Legal and Product and needs to be resolved before launch.",
  "fix_options": [
    "Product and Finance ask StreamLedger, VerifyPoint and Harbor Analytics to move processing of our customer data to a UK or EEA region, and confirm the change before launch.",
    "Finance and Product replace any supplier that cannot process customer data within the UK or EEA with one that can, starting with Harbor Analytics (V003), which also has no signed DPA (C-2025-020).",
    "Legal reviews whether the customer terms can be changed to permit US processing, with customer agreement, and gets the missing Harbor Analytics DPA signed. Until the terms change, the current UK/EEA promise still applies."
  ]
}
```
